  lex_digraphs.pcpp - Lexical compliance: digraphs

  C++'s digraphs work everywhere, PaskalCPP code included (BNF.md sec 9):
  <: :> are [ ], <% %> are { }, %: and %:%: are # and ## (a %: first on its
  line starts a preprocessor line). <:: is < then :: (C++11), so
  std::vector<::std::int32_t> is a vector of int32.

  How to check, from repo\bin:
    pcpp res\tests\lex_digraphs.pcpp -r
    pcpp res\tests\lex_digraphs.pcpp -r -t x86_64-linux-gnu   (runs in WSL)
  EXPECT:
    index 5
    vector 3
    paste 21
    macro 42
    [Heap] Allocs: 0, Frees: 0, Leaked: 0
  EXITCODE: 0
  The [Heap] line is the debug build's heap report.

  Break it: run each file below the same way, without -r; each reports
  exactly what the // comment on its marked line says, and nothing else:
    lex_digraphs_err_hash.pcpp
      a %: that is not first on its line (LX0008)
*******************************************************************************/

module exe lex_digraphs;

%:include <vector>
%:define TWICE(x) ((x) * 2)
%:define CAT(a, b) a%:%:b

std::vector<::std::int32_t> GNums<%1, 2, 3%>;
int CAT(my, value) = 21;

var
  LA: array[0..2] of int32;

begin
  LA<:1:> := 5;
  println("index {}", LA<:1:>);
  println("vector {}", GNums<:2:>);
  println("paste {}", myvalue);
  println("macro {}", TWICE(myvalue));
end.
